# Module: Audit Logging

## Policy

**Everything significant is logged.** Full spec: `docs/universal-logging-policy.md`

## Key Entities

`AuditLog` — append-only, immutable, no delete API

## Extended Action Enum

```
Create | Update | Delete | Read | Export | Login | LoginFailed | Logout
TokenRefresh | PasswordChange | PermissionChange | AccessDenied
StatusChange | BulkUpdate | BulkDelete | Reverse | Post
EventPublished | EventConsumed | EventFailed | JobStarted | JobCompleted | JobFailed
SuperAdminAction | Impersonation | Failed
```

## Categories

`Auth`, `Rbac`, `Institution`, `Student`, `Attendance`, `Fee`, `Finance`, `Lms`, `Notification`, `Report`, `Social`, `Platform`, `System`

## Permissions

```
audit.logs.read
audit.logs.export
audit.logs.read-all-tenant    # tenant admin — own tenant only
audit.logs.read-platform      # super admin — cross-tenant
```

## Pipeline Behaviors

| Behavior | Triggers On |
|---|---|
| `AuditBehavior` | All `ICommand` (writes) |
| `AuditReadBehavior` | Queries marked `[AuditRead]` or in `ReadAuditEntities` config |
| `AuthorizationBehavior` | Logs `AccessDenied` on 403 |
| `RequestLoggingMiddleware` | Every HTTP request (Serilog) |

## Key Services

- `IAuditService` / `AuditLogService` — write audit entries
- `IAccessAuditService` — sensitive read + export logging
- `EntityChangeCaptureInterceptor` — EF before/after on Update

## APIs

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/v1/audit-logs` | List with filters |
| GET | `/api/v1/audit-logs/{id}` | Detail |
| GET | `/api/v1/audit-logs/export` | CSV export (itself audited) |
| GET | `/api/v1/audit-logs/entity/{type}/{id}` | History for one entity |

## Storage & Retention

- Index: `(tenant_id, created_at DESC)`, `(entity_type, entity_id)`, `(user_id, created_at)`
- Financial audits: 7-year minimum retention
- Phase 2: monthly partitioning + cold archive

## Do NOT

- Expose delete/update endpoints for audit logs
- Bypass audit for super-admin (they get `SuperAdminAction` category instead)
- Recursively audit audit writes
